        "finalMessage": "I fixed issue 1 (no-nested-ternary at line 119) in `ExplorerNavNotebooks.tsx`. I didn't run the linter, as instructed.\n\nThe nested ternary inside the JSX chose between three things: a loading skeleton, a \"no notebooks\" message, or the notebook list. That choice is now an `if` / `else if` / `else` block before the `return`, which sets a `content` variable. The JSX renders `{content}` inside the same `div`.\n\nThe behavior is the same: the conditions are checked in the same order and each branch renders the same element with the same props. The simple ternary that picks the empty-state message was never nested, so I left it alone.\n\nI typed `content` as `JSX.Element` rather than `React.ReactNode`. This file has no React types available, and `stubs.tsx` declares the global `JSX` namespace.",
